# 0001 — Five samples draw from the unseeded `kotlin.random.Random`, so every render of them is a
# different picture: `BorderSampleWithDynamicData` (initial width, shape and gradient colours),
# `SimpleFlowRow_EqualHeight` / `SimpleFlowColumn_EqualWidth` (random strings of random length) and
# `ContextualFlowRow_ItemPosition` / `ContextualFlowColumn_ItemPosition` (random item widths and
# heights). The preview-diff bot then reports all five as Changed on every PR whatever it touched —
# m3-catalog#554 changed only ui-builder policy files and still flagged the set — which trains a
# reader to skip the Changed section, the one thing that bot is for.
#
# The fix SEEDS the randomness rather than removing it, so each sample still demonstrates what
# upstream wrote it to show (items of uneven size, a border that changes on click). The flow samples
# seed per item, by the item index the layout already hands the lambda, so the value is stable
# across recompositions and independent of how many previews ran before it in the same JVM; a single
# shared seeded `Random` would not be. `generateRandomString` takes the `Random` as a defaulted
# parameter so any other caller is unaffected. The border sample seeds one remembered `Random(0)`
# and keeps using it in the click handlers, so its buttons still produce new widths, shapes and
# colours in a live render.
#
# Not a version skew: upstream has no reason to make a demo deterministic. Re-cut it if upstream
# rewrites any of these five functions.
